I'm sure we all appreciate that the mac interface is not complete, so I intend
my comments to be suggestions, not criticisms (as, I'm sure, everybody else
does too).

I certainly like the message box being movable/resizable as I play NH on a
number of different Mac's with different screen sizes. It's really nice to have
a large message box and not to have to press something for --more-- every three
lines or so (beartraps become _almost_ bearable - sorry about the pun).

Having the character stats as a separate box is useless (IMHO) unless you can
reshape it. i.e. make it tall and thin instead of short and wide. When playing
Mac nethack, all mac monitors (except maybe 10 inch) have a wasted space down
the side(s), since the dungeon is never as wide as the screen (I normally put
my inventory here, so that it doesn't overlap much of the dungeon window).
So I recon it would be great if we could list the character stats down, say,
the left hand side of the screen. i.e.

------------ -----------------------------------------------------------------
|= Stats ==| |========================= Dungeon =============================|
|----------- -----------------------------------------------------------------
| Name     | |                                                               |
| Class    | |                                                               |
| Level    | |
|          | |
| STR ##   | |
| INT ##   | |
...

Just like in Moria, I think. Other combinations are left as an exercise to the
student.

Also, may I add my vote to the "permanantly open inventory" debate. This would be
cool.

I don't like the new pull-down menu's - the ones in 3.1.1 were better. To make
them less crowded, I think you can use ResEdit to put an extra space in front
of all the menu names, but I haven't tried it. I also tried to use ResEdit to
resize the boxes containing the class, sex and play mode, but they still only
displayed the first letter.

Otherwise the new version is cool by me. Many thanks to the dev team.


